\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 DR. RICHARD BESSER, FORMER ACTING DIRECTOR, CDC: You know, Sara, I practiced pediatrics for more than 30 years, and nothing I did as a pediatrician had more proven value than making sure that my patients were vaccinated fully and on time. And that required a lot of time talking to parents, listening to their questions, answering their questions. So, when you have the president of the United States, who has absolutely no medical or scientific background, putting out an executive order that changes the well-constructed evidence-based vaccine schedule, instilling fear in people, something really, really bad can happen. Parents who want to do the right thing may make the wrong choice for their children, and that can be devastating.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 SIDNER: Has there been any change in any of the research, any of the sort of medical efficacy, anything that has changed in order that the president can hang his hat on, or is the only change that has happened is that his HHS secretary is skeptical of vaccines?}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 BESSER: Well, you know, we have an HHS secretary, RFK Jr., who is one of the nation's leading anti-vaccine advocates. He tried to put in this schedule back in January. He issued it from the department. He didn't go through the process that Congress put in place to ensure that our vaccine recommendations are solid, our evidence-based, that our vaccines are safe.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 So, he launched this in January. It was challenged in the court by the American Academy of Pediatrics, I'm a member, as well as other groups. And a judge said, no, you can't do this.}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}
\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0
\ulnone\cf2 So, this is another attempt to put in the secretary's anti-vaccine agenda. I expect that the courts won't accept it. But that doesn't mean there won't be damage. Because whenever you politicize these decisions and take them away from well thought decisions and conversations that parents have with their doctors, with their nurses, with their pharmacists, you're going to -- you're going to get into a situation where children suffer.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 SIDNER: Yes. What is interesting is that the president is putting these out as a directive, and not once I -- did I hear him say, you know, talk to your doctor, because the ultimate thing is for you to spend time with your doctor, to talk it through with a medical professional who went to school and practices. He's just making these claims.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 I do want to read one of them that really stood out to me and was shocking, frankly. He said, "I've seen proof of where they have a vaccination that looks like the size of a bottle of soda poured into a little child's body, and bad things happen in many cases. In too many cases."}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Have you ever seen a size of a bottle being poured into a child when it comes to the MMR vaccine, which is what he was referring to?}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum
\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 BESSER: Yes, this is -- this is yet another one of the president's lies. You know, the amount of material that you inject with a vaccine is a fraction of a -- of a teaspoon. So, where he's coming up with these ideas, it's utter nonsense, and it will instill fear.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 [08:40:01]}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 You know, he's -- he called for dividing the measles, mumps, rubella shot into three separate shots.}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0
\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 SIDNER: Right.}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0
\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 BESSER: There's no health benefit in doing that. And it's going to require parents to take off three days from work instead of just one. A lot of people don't have personal time. You know, when you take your child to the doctor, you're taking time off work. A lot of people then aren't earning income for that.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 If there's a health benefit, that's a different question. But this is a vaccine that we've been giving since the 1970s. Highly effective and safe. As a pediatrician, I loved when we were able to give combined vaccines because, you know, I've yet to meet a child who really likes to get a vaccine. And so, if you can reduce the number, and parents as well don't like to give their kids a lot of shots. So, if you can reduce the number by combining and ensuring that they're still safe and effective, that's a real win.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 SIDNER: I do have to ask you lastly, ask you, I'm sorry about this, just a few seconds more. Just quickly, does it exist right now where you can get those shots separately? Because, like you said, since the 70s, this has been a cocktail that has been given to children and has been incredibly effective. It is only now when people aren't taking it that we're seeing a huge explosion of measles. It has been deadly in some states, like Texas. So, do these individual shots exist right now?}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 BESSER: Yes, so, they don't exist in this country. They would have to be licensed. They're available in some other countries. So, they would have to go through licensure in the U.S. And your point is a good one. At a time when we are seeing -- in the past 18 months we saw more measles cases than we saw in the previous 25 years combined. What you want to see is a president coming on TV and saying, if you haven't had your child vaccinated against measles, go out and do it right now, because this is spreading around our country and there's something you can do to keep your child safe. Instead, he's instilling more fear than -- and that will lead some people to do the wrong thing for the children's health.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 SIDNER: Dr. Richard Besser, it is good to have you to give us a science-based evidence for these particular shots. Thank you so much. I do appreciate your time this morning.}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard
