\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 BERMAN: So on, you know, these data centers, if they are going to be built, how do people want to see it done?}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0
\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 ENTEN: You know, one of the key nuggets that those who want the data centers to be built will say is, we have to stay ahead of China when it comes to tech, right? So, there's a great poll question that essentially formulated this, right? Americans on building A.I. data centers. Slowly to address local concerns, of which there have been many, or quickly to maintain a tech edge over, you know, folks like -- places in China. And on this one, it is a four to one clear blowout. I mean we're talking about 78 percent of Americans, voters say slowly to address local concerns. Just one in five, 21 percent, say quickly to maintain the edge over China.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 And again, what we see is across all of the different political and demographic groups, everyone agrees that they should be built slowly to address local concerns. And so, when we start off at the top saying, hey, there is this debate, there really isn't much of a debate when it comes to the politics of it. The vast majority of Americans in basically every single camp are in agreement on this, they want it to be slowly to address those local concerns.}
