\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 And a former flight attendant from Canada has pleaded guilty in U.S. federal court to wire fraud for pretending to be a pilot. The U.S. attorney's office in Hawaii says this man, Dallas Pokornik, used a fake employee I.D. card and experienced as a, well, he pretended to be a pilot, but as an attendant. He did that because he wanted to get hundreds of free flights on three different airlines. And he did it over the course of four years. He even gained access to the jump seat and cockpits. He posted pictures of his fake high-flying lifestyle on Facebook for all to see. Wonder how he got busted. Prosecutors say he now faces up to 20 years in prison. There is no flying in his future, John.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 BERMAN: All right, new this morning, a CNN investigation. A Russian- born American citizen shot and killed by the FBI hundreds of miles from his home. And the agency will not officially say why.}{\rtlch\afs24
\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2
